  "title": "Veterinary Clinical Trials Network | Johns Hopkins Radiology",
  "text": "Veterinary Clinical Trials Network | Johns Hopkins Radiology\nSkip to Main Content\nJohns Hopkins Medicine\nMenu\nHealth\nSchool of Medicine\nJohns Hopkins Medicine Home\nAbout\nPatient Care\nResearch\nMyChart\nSchedule an Appointment\nFind a Doctor\nFind a Clinical Trial\nPay Your Bill\nEmployment\nClose\nSearch\nSearch\nJohns Hopkins Medicine\nSearch\nClose\nMyChart Login\nMyChart\nRadiology and Radiological Science\nRadiology and Radiological Science\nMenu\nRadiology and Radiological Science\nMain Menu\nHome\nClinical Specialties\nEducation\nEducation\nBack\nto Radiology and Radiological Science Main Menu\nOverview\nResidency\nResidency\nBack\nto Education\nOverview\nMeet the Team\nApplication Process\nDiagnostic Radiology Residency\nNuclear Medicine Residency\nInterventional Radiology Residency\nResidency Fellowship Verification Requests\nMeet Our Residents\nMeet Our Alumni\nFellowships\nMaster's in Medical Physics\nTechnologist Programs\nMedical Student Elective\nMRI Technologist Training Program\nCT Technologist Training Program\nAlumni Information\nResearch\nResearch\nBack\nto Radiology and Radiological Science Main Menu\nOverview\nResearch Divisions\nResearch Divisions\nBack\nto Research\nOverview\nCancer Imaging Research\nMagnetic Resonance Research\nRadiological Physics Division\nResearch Labs and Centers\nService Cores\nReferring Veterinarians\nReferring Veterinarians\nBack\nto Research Divisions\nVeterinary Clinical Trials Network\nVeterinarians\nPatient Information\nPatient Information\nBack\nto Radiology and Radiological Science Main Menu\nOverview\nAppointments\nImages and Reports\nTreatment Centers\nTreatment Centers\nBack\nto Patient Information\nHereditary Hemorrhagic Telangiectasia Center\nNuclear Medicine Radiotheranostic Center\nLocations and Services\nReferring Provider Information\nOur Team\nOur Team\nBack\nto Radiology and Radiological Science Main Menu\nOur Leadership\nOur Team\nOur Legacy\nTechnologist Recruiting\nFaculty Recruiting\nNews and Events\nNews and Events\nBack\nto Radiology and Radiological Science Main Menu\nOverview\nAwards and Achievements\nRadiologyUpdate Newsletter\nWays to Give\nVeterinary Radiology For Your Pets\nWe offer a range of veterinary radiology services including MRI, veterinary anesthesia, radiation therapy and t\nransarterial embolization\nfor cats and dogs. We work with both pet owners and referring veterinarians to provide exceptional care for your pet.\nMake an Appointment\nMake an appointment for imaging services for veterinary patients at our location in Baltimore, Maryland.\nEmail Us\nAbout Us\nOur Services\nClinical Trials\nContact Information\nWhat We Do\nPartner with our pet owners and referring veterinarians to preserve the human-animal bond through veterinary radiology.\nProvide superior veterinary clinical trial services by maintaining the gold standard in the veterinary clinical trials arena.\nEducate pet owners, veterinarians, researchers and physicians about the roles they play in keeping pets happy and healthy.\nFoster academic and community growth to ensure our clinical trials lead in the practice of safe, innovative, efficient and beneficial veterinary care.\nOur Veterinary Radiology Services\nWe are located in Baltimore, Maryland.\nVeterinary Anesthesia\nImage-Guided Tissue Biopsy\nRadiosynoviorthesis\nComputed tomography (CT scan)\nCone-beam CT\nCT angiography (CTA)\nRadiation Therapy\n(Yttrium-90/Y-90)\nFluoroscopy\nLiver scan\nLung scan\nMagnetic resonance angiography (MRA)\nMagnetic resonance imaging (MRI--1.5T and 3T)\nMyelogram\nPositron emission tomography (PET scan) and PET/CT\nSpiral CT\nSPECT-CT\nTransarterial Embolization and Chemoembolization\nWhole-body cancer scan\nVeterinary Anesthesia\nOur Expertise\nVCTN has state-of-the-art anesthetic equipment. It is the combination of experience, expertise, a highly skilled team and cutting-edge equipment that minimizes the inherent risks associated with sedation and anesthesia. Each veterinary patient’s well-being is the most important factor for all procedures at VCTN.\nLearn more\nOur Director\nRebecca Krimins, D.V.M., M.S.\nDr. Krimins\nis a residency-trained veterinary anesthesiologist and has anesthetized thousands of animals undergoing advanced imaging procedures. Her specialty in veterinary anesthesia, sedation and pain management in combination with her experience in directing advanced clinical research offers each veterinary patient the best opportunities for diagnosis and therapy.\nAs founder and director of the Veterinary Clinical Trials Network at Johns Hopkins University, Dr. Krimins has built a revolutionary center designed to leverage the expertise and platforms available at Johns Hopkins University in order to transform newly discovered diagnostics and therapeutics into real-life practical approaches that benefit veterinary patients.\nOur Pets\nSubmission from Isabella G.\nClinical Trials for Veterinary Imaging\nCanine Cancer Clinical Trial\nThis clinical trial will enroll a total of 5-7 dogs in order to confirm that\n18\nF DCFPyl PET-CT offers an improved sensitivity for the early detection of hemangiosarcoma cancer or metastatic prostate cancer.\nCanine Metastatic Cancer Clinical Trial\nThis\nclinical trial\nwill enroll 5-10 dogs to evaluate the efficacy of a novel chemotherapeutic agent called IF7-SN38. This trial includes dogs with metastatic disease. This chemotherapy is delivered intravenously as a series, every other day for three to five days.\nCanine Brain Cancer Clinical Trial\nThis\nclinical trial\nwill enroll 5-10 dogs to evaluate the efficacy of a novel chemotherapeutic agent called IF7-SN38. This chemotherapy is delivered intravenously as a series, every other day for three to five days.\nComing Soon\nCanine Prostate Cancer\nReceive the latest VCTN updates\nSign up\nContact Information\n720 Rutland Ave.\nRoss Building #315\nBaltimore, Maryland 21205\nTelephone:\n410-614-0105\nEmail:\n[email protected]\nSee More\nRadiology and Radiological Science\nHome\nClinical Specialties\nEducation\nResearch\nPatient Information\nOur Team\nNews and Events\nRequest an Appointment:\n443-997-7237\nLanguage Assistance Available:\nEspañol\nአማርኛ\n繁體中文\nFrançais\nTagalog\nРусский\nPortuguês\nItaliano\nTiếng Việt\nƁàsɔ́ɔ̀-wùɖù-po-nyɔ̀\nIgbo asusu\nèdè Yorùbá\nবাংলা\n日本語\n한국어\nKreyòl Ayisyen\nالعربية\nDeutsch\nPolski\nΕλληνικά\nગુજરાતી\nภาษาไทย\nاُردُو\nفارسی\nहिंदी\nDeitsch\nខ្មែរ\nContact & Privacy Information\nContact Johns Hopkins Medicine\nPrice Transparency\n|\nPatient Care Locations\nNotice of Privacy Practices\n|\nPrivacy Statement\nTerms & Conditions of Use\n|\nNon-Discrimination Notice\nManage Cookie Preferences\nCopyright ©\n2026\nThe Johns Hopkins University, The Johns Hopkins Hospital, and Johns Hopkins Health System. All rights reserved.",
